# region contracts
# The contracts of `project clean` that later regions read (T004): its caps,
# the Git floor, the key order of each JSON object, the closed code sets and
# the human text. Sources: specs/004-project-clean-all-safe/data-model.md and
# contracts/project-clean.md, and design.md D14 and D18 of
# openspec/changes/add-project-clean-all-safe/, whose spec deltas govern where
# they differ. Nothing here reads TIMING (lead ruling R-29); a time that D18
# prints is its literal text. A change to a key or a code goes through the lead.

# Caps and bounds, never scaled by a test. `worktree_rows` is the row cap of
# each plan mode; the first five keys are the plan's `limits` object. A
# target's revalidation spawns at most six Git children, seven where the plan
# read the repository's extensions.worktreeConfig as true (design D7 and D14;
